# Obsidian AI Agent Plugin Direct Google Cloud Vertex AI Integration

Architecture pattern for connecting Obsidian desktop plugins (e.g. `ai-agent`) directly to Google Cloud Vertex AI with automatic token refresh, zero background daemons, and multi-model Gemini selection.

## 1. Authentication Architecture (Zero Background Daemons)

Instead of running an external local proxy daemon (like Python or Node on port 8765/5199), desktop plugins running in Electron/Node can manage token lifecycle directly:

1. **Primary Auth Path: ADC Refresh Token Exchange (Fastest, ~200ms)**
   - Read `~/.config/gcloud/application_default_credentials.json`.
   - If present with `client_id`, `client_secret`, and `refresh_token`:
   - POST to `https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token`:
     ```json
     {
       "client_id": "<client_id>",
       "client_secret": "<client_secret>",
       "refresh_token": "<refresh_token>",
       "grant_type": "refresh_token"
     }
     ```
   - Returns `{ "access_token": "ya29...", "expires_in": 3599 }`.
   - Cache token in-memory and refresh automatically when expiration is within 5 minutes or on HTTP 401.

2. **Secondary Auth Path: Direct `gcloud` Execution with Path Probing**
   - In Electron desktop environments (macOS Finder launch), `process.env.PATH` is often minimal (`/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin`).
   - Probe candidate paths:
     - `/opt/homebrew/bin/gcloud` (Apple Silicon)
     - `/usr/local/bin/gcloud` (Intel macOS)
     - `~/google-cloud-sdk/bin/gcloud`
   - Execute `gcloud auth print-access-token`.

3. **Fallback: Service Account JSON Key**
   - Allow user to paste a service account JSON file.
   - Mint JWT signed with RS256 and exchange at `https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token`.

## 2. Vertex AI Endpoint & Payload Normalization Rules

### Endpoint Construction
```text
https://aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1beta1/projects/{projectId}/locations/{location}/publishers/google/models/{model}:{action}
```
- For standard generation: `:generateContent`
- For streaming: `:streamGenerateContent?alt=sse`
- Location: `locations/global` is mandatory for Gemini 3.8 (`gemini-3.8-flash`) and Gemini 4 (`gemini-4-argon`). Calling regional endpoints like `us-central1` returns HTTP 404.

### Headers
```http
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN>
Content-Type: application/json
```
*(CRITICAL: Do NOT send `x-goog-api-key` to `aiplatform.googleapis.com` when Bearer token is present, as it triggers HTTP 401).*

### Critical Payload Normalization Quirks
1. **Gemini Function Calling API Turn Balance (HTTP 400 Mismatch)**:
   - Error: `[400] Please ensure that the number of function response parts is equal to the number of function call parts of the function call turn.`
   - In Vertex AI Gemini chat history, every turn containing $N$ `functionCall` parts MUST be immediately followed by a turn containing exactly $N$ matching `functionResponse` parts.
   - If an execution was interrupted, aborted, or the user sent a new turn before tool responses were appended, sanitize `parsedBody.contents` before submitting:
   ```javascript
   if (Array.isArray(parsedBody.contents)) {
     let origContents = parsedBody.contents;
     let newContents = [];
     for (let i = 0; i < origContents.length; i++) {
       let turn = origContents[i];
       newContents.push(turn);
       if (turn && turn.role === "model" && Array.isArray(turn.parts)) {
         let fnCalls = turn.parts.filter(p => p && p.functionCall).map(p => p.functionCall);
         if (fnCalls.length > 0) {
           let nextTurn = (i + 1 < origContents.length) ? origContents[i + 1] : null;
           let nextParts = (nextTurn && Array.isArray(nextTurn.parts)) ? nextTurn.parts : [];
           let fnResps = nextParts.filter(p => p && p.functionResponse).map(p => p.functionResponse);
           if (nextTurn && (nextTurn.role === "user" || nextTurn.role === "function") && fnResps.length > 0) {
             let existingNames = fnResps.map(r => r.name);
             for (let fc of fnCalls) {
               if (!existingNames.includes(fc.name)) {
                 nextParts.push({ functionResponse: { name: fc.name, response: { result: "completed" } } });
                 existingNames.push(fc.name);
               }
             }
             while (nextParts.filter(p => p && p.functionResponse).length < fnCalls.length) {
               nextParts.push({ functionResponse: { name: fnCalls[0].name || "tool", response: { result: "completed" } } });
             }
             nextTurn.parts = nextParts;
           } else {
             let synParts = fnCalls.map(fc => ({ functionResponse: { name: fc.name || "tool", response: { result: "completed" } } }));
             newContents.push({ role: "user", parts: synParts });
           }
         }
       }
     }
     parsedBody.contents = newContents;
   }
   ```

2. **Thinking Config Compatibility**:
   - `gemini-2.5-flash` and `gemini-2.5-pro` reject `thinkingConfig.thinkingLevel`. Sending `thinkingLevel: "low"|"high"` results in:
     `HTTP 400 Unable to submit request because thinking_level is not supported by this model`.
   - `thinkingLevel` is only supported on Gemini 3.x series (`gemini-3.7-flash`, `gemini-3-flash-preview`). Strip `thinkingLevel` when targeting non-3.x models.

3. **Suggested Models List**:
   - `gemini-3.8-flash`: SOTA Fast & Intelligent, default for agentic chat and UI extensions.
   - `gemini-4-argon`: Next-Gen flagship reasoning model.
   - `gemini-2.5-flash`: Fast fallback.
   - `gemini-2.5-pro`: Deep reasoning & coding.
